  "query_preview": "..\nTyphoon Choi-wan has steadily moved northeast today, moving away \nfrom the far northern Mariana Islands. All tropical storm and typhoon\nwatches and warnings have ended and Typhoon Choi-wan will continue \nto move away from the region. In its place the monsoon surge will \nremain draped over the Marianas. A relative lull in shower activity \nis expected tonight through Tuesday with isolated to low-end (30%) \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms. The wet phase of the \nmonsoon is expected to return Tuesday night as the monsoon \nreorganizes. There is potential for another round of heavy rainfall \nduring the second half of this week and a hydrological products may \nbe necessary. Another lull looks to develop late this weekend.",
